/*  The consumer, and the point of the pair: it names ONE book.

    `pennies` pulls `math` in its own file, so this program never mentions it. Compare ledger.cufe,
    which has to nest `Pull a book on math.` around `Pull a bookkeeping.` because `bookkeeping`
    leaves that name open — there, the dependency is part of the spelling; here it is not.

    ★ Pulling resolves BESIDE THE FILE THAT PULLS, so `pennies` is found next to this one with no
    project, no configuration and no path. A `books/` folder at a project root is the second place
    it looks, not the first.  */

Pull a book on pennies.
    Define prices as a series of number with (3.514, 24.99, 8.252).

    For each item in prices, repeat:
        State "item:    {item}".
    Done.

    State "".
    State "rounded: {cast pennies's total on (prices)}".
Done.
